## 2. `player_multikill_stat`

| Column | Must mean | The reading that looks right and isn't |
|---|---|---|
| `steamid64` | The player | — |
| `kills` | Kills **in a single round**, 2–5 | Not kills in a time window. A 3k is three kills in one round, however far apart |
| `count` | How many rounds ended with that many kills | — |

**One row per (player, level, season) with a counter**, not one row per event —
that is what the existing schema shape suggests, and it is the right one: the
site wants "how many aces has Kurt had", not a list.

**To confirm:** are team kills excluded? They must be, for the same reason as in
the daily-stat contract — a TK inflating a multikill is nonsense. And does a
grenade that kills three at once count as a 3k? We would say yes; it is one
round and three kills. Say if the plugin counts it differently.

