## 4. Knife and taser kills — a table that does not exist yet

The rarest and most-told moments on a CS server, and worth keeping forever
*because* they are rare: a couple a day is a thousand rows a year. Storage is
not the constraint here; nothing is.

| Column | Must mean |
|---|---|
| `killer_steamid64` | — |
| `victim_steamid64` | — |
| `weapon` | knife / taser / which knife |
| `mapname`, `stamp`, `match_id` | Where and when |

**Two SteamIDs in one row, which means two things.**

First, both belong on the erasure list, on both columns. A row naming only the
killer would leave the victim standing after their erasure — exactly how
`player_weapon_shots` came to leak.

Second, and this is a decision OSWeb has already taken: **the site will never
build a leaderboard of victims.** A single event with two names is a story
people tell each other; a ranking of who has been knifed most is a permanent
record of someone's humiliation, and this site praises rather than embarrasses.
Individual rows get both names. Aggregates only ever count the dealer.

Nothing is asked of OSBase for that beyond recording both — but it explains why
the victim column matters and why it is not there to rank anyone.

